+## 5. Full gate re-run (additional check)
+
+A full `sh tests/run-all.sh` at canonical HEAD `36bd30d7` exited **1**, but not at the
+test named in the report: it stopped at `tests/mission-boundary-smoke.sh` after 83 test scripts,
+all of which had passed — including `executive-cycle-smoke.sh` ("Independent Executive dispatch
+and fail-closed assignment smoke passed", exit 0). Tracing the failure with `sh -x` showed the
+grep for mission-specific text in `government/` found nothing; the failing assertion was
+`[ ! -e government/pnp ]`. `/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche/government/pnp` is a **local, untracked,
+git-ignored directory containing only `__pycache__`** (Python bytecode cache, created
+2026-11-23): `git ls-files government/pnp` is empty and `git status --short government/pnp` is
+clean. In a clean worktree at the same HEAD, `mission-boundary-smoke.sh` and
+`executive-cycle-smoke.sh` both exit 0. The full-suite failure is therefore a local checkout
+artifact, not a committed gate defect and not the blocker the Executive reported. A full
+clean-worktree suite re-run then completed: `sh tests/run-all.sh` in the clean worktree at the
+same HEAD ran 108 test scripts and exited **0** ("All Viche tests passed"). This independently
+establishes that the Act 31 delivery gate is green in a clean checkout at canonical HEAD and
+that the canonical-checkout failure was a local artifact. No conclusion in sections 1–4 depends
+on this supplementary check; it removes the residual doubt about the broad "no `tests/`
+delivery can pass" claim.
